{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22754511","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.22754511","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.22754511","identifiers":[],"alternateIdentifiers":[],"creators":[{"name":"Song, Zhouran","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zhouran","familyName":"Song","affiliation":["Independent Researcher"],"nameIdentifiers":[{"nameIdentifier":"0009-0001-2985-0012","nameIdentifierScheme":"ORCID"}]}],"titles":[{"title":"Keel: event-sourced runtime and logs for the economics of recovery in LLM agent workflows"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"LLM agents"},{"subject":"reliability"},{"subject":"fault tolerance"},{"subject":"checkpointing"},{"subject":"cost analysis"},{"subject":"event sourcing"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-09-14","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"COMP","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"SoftwareSourceCode","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Software"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsSupplementTo","relatedIdentifier":"https://github.com/szrusca/keel-recovery-artifact/tree/v1.0.4","resourceTypeGeneral":"Software","relatedIdentifierType":"URL"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22754512","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22758524","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22757813","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22758172","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"v1.0.4","rightsList":[{"rights":"MIT License","rightsUri":"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"mit","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Artifact for the paper \"The Economics of Recovery: Measuring What Retry, Rollback, and Escalation Buy in Long-Horizon LLM Agent Workflows\" (manuscript under review).\n\nKeel is an event-sourced runtime for LLM agent workflows: every model call, verification, retry, checkpoint, rollback, escalation, and budget event is an append-only record carrying provider, model, reasoning setting, token counts, latency, HTTP status, error class, and list-price cost.\n\nThis archive contains the runtime (pure Python standard library), the complete event log of the study (about 41,000 model calls across eleven free API tiers), per-run summaries, the analysis scripts that regenerate every table and figure in the paper, and the run logs, including the provider outages observed during the study. Two synthetic but programmatically verifiable task families are included: T1, an integer ledger, and T2, a warehouse order state machine.\n\nContents: ledger/ (runtime and analysis code), runs/ (raw event logs and summaries), results/ (analysis outputs), logs/ (stdout of every run).\n\nLicensing: code in ledger/ and check_keys.py is under the MIT License; event logs and analysis outputs in runs/, results/, and logs/ are under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md).\n\nNo API keys are included. Reproduction instructions are in README.md.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"If you use this software or data, please cite it as below.","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22754511","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":5,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":4,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-09-14T16:21:15.000Z","registered":"2026-09-14T16:21:15.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-09-14T21:16:18.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"da